00:06:13,334 --> 00:06:21,873
%ar)', gitk --all (a window), the network or commit graph views on GitHub, or your editor's Git panel.

93
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:25,125
Let me try something.

94
00:06:25,125 --> 00:06:32,158
Draw the graph without --all from the side branch and conclude, wrongly, that main has nothing new:

95
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:37,253
Without --all, git log draws only what is reachable from HEAD.

96
00:06:37,253 --> 00:06:44,083
From feature-tea, the opening hours and the merge on main are invisible, although they exist.

97
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:45,919
Same lesson as lesson 13:

98
00:06:45,919 --> 00:06:48,490
a view is not the whole repository.

99
00:06:50,233 --> 00:06:52,033
Here is the fix.

100
00:06:53,767 --> 00:06:54,480
Got it.

101
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,231
What do I need to remember?

102
00:06:57,767 --> 00:06:59,174
History is a graph:

103
00:06:59,174 --> 00:07:03,841
commits point to their parents; branches are labels on commits.

104
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:10,205
git log --oneline --graph --all draws the whole graph; --first-parent follows the main line.

105
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:15,116
A merge commit has two parents; the first commit has none.
